M4.1: PCI enumeration - the storage estate on the bus

- pci.c: type-1 config access (0xCF8/0xCFC), bus-0 walk with the
  standard multifunction rule (probe fn 1..7 only when hdr_type bit 7
  says so), fixed device table (vid/did/class/hdr/irq pin+line/6 BARs)
  that M4.2's AHCI driver will search by class. Width-limited hex
  printer for VID:DID readability; storage-class devices print their
  BARs.
- main.c: pci_init() after the heap test, before interrupts.
- Test bench update: future M4 boots add '-device ich9-ahci,id=ahci'
  to put a real AHCI HBA on the piix3 bus (the boot drive stays
  if=ide, so the boot chain is untouched).

Evidence (QEMU): 7 devices, all textbook for a pc machine:
  00:00.0 host bridge (8086:1237), 00:01.0 PIIX3 ISA (0601),
  00:01.1 IDE (010180, BAR4=0xC060 port-IO bus-master regs),
  00:01.3 PM (0680, irq 9), 00:02.0 VGA (1234:1111),
  00:03.0 e1000 (0200), and the target -
  00:04.0 8086:2922 class 010601 = ICH9 AHCI, BAR4=0xC041 (I/O idx),
  BAR5=0xFEBF1000 (MMIO HBA; above the 1 GiB identity map - M4.2 must
  map it into the demand region via explicit page tables).
Multifunction probing proved itself: PIIX3's fn .1/.3 exist only
because the walk honors the hdr_type bit.
